# Line endings.
#
# Windows traditionally ends every line with two invisible characters (CRLF);
# Mac, Linux, and the GitHub Actions runner use one (LF). Git can translate
# between them, which is what the "this file uses LF but Git will convert to
# CRLF" warning was about.
#
# GitHub Desktop's default was `* text=auto`, which stores LF in the repo but
# hands you CRLF locally. That works, but it means the files on this machine
# never quite match the files the nightly scraper writes on GitHub's Linux
# runner — which shows up as noise when reviewing diffs.
#
# `eol=lf` keeps LF everywhere: in the repo, on this machine, and in CI.
# One format, no translation, no warning. VS Code handles LF without noticing.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats — never translate these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
